    "summary": "This sword’s blade is straight near the tip and transitions into gentle undulations toward the lower half. The guard consists of pierced <em>okir</em> wings, secured on one side by a single <em>asang-asang</em> clamp (also called <em>baca-baca</em> by the Maranao). The hilt is wrapped in dark fiber or rattan bindings and metal ferrules, and fitted with a small, comparatively modest cockatoo (<em>kakatua</em>) form.",
